 ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\text{ }i+(2y{x}^{3}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+2yzk \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,-1,1) & =3(1)^{2}(-1)^{2}\\text{ }i+(\\,2(-1)(1)^{3}+(1)^{2}\\,)\\text{ }j+2(-1)(1)k \\\\  & =3\\,i-1\\,j-2k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨3,-1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80764/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80764"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80768/selection/fb11ed16db22f9caf43f16cbc33e8d4ef6fa57185b71dedd2e5f5bdcff1a4bed" :answer/id #uuid "d1a0204f-79f2-59c1-9f92-f3a205e0127f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80768/selection/3d239971f701225e791ff0bcdd4bdbd8bef4c1b081f9da88053487ec8a0837ed" :answer/id #uuid "20e97979-252b-55b7-9d46-84e022f412c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80768/selection/571bcbf12f6a2964e059e116f565f7dccd4591b2bb38c1f98f007a9fa19b05de" :answer/id #uuid "42785da6-5579-54a8-beb3-49d7c936bba3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y+2,\\,z-2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80768/selection/e5decc4150b760914cd0c276e29446374cd13b1976fc3c6778f33780269e9ce2" :answer/id #uuid "33c40942-7dd8-5c4a-88d3-1b6dd932fb15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80768/selection/1a2acfe5467bf9da155108d16669be8bf540403d734f98797845fdbd32db81c2" :answer/id #uuid "5717cf5a-c402-58fd-a7f8-535c5ba5d798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80768/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb3d1b51-54b4-5b76-8be0-51d70939c33e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80768/selection/1a2acfe5467bf9da155108d16669be8bf540403d734f98797845fdbd32db81c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-80768/selection/fb11ed16db22f9caf43f16cbc33e8d4ef6fa57185b71dedd2e5f5bdcff1a4bed" "q-80768/selection/3d239971f701225e791ff0bcdd4bdbd8bef4c1b081f9da88053487ec8a0837ed" "q-80768/selection/571bcbf12f6a2964e059e116f565f7dccd4591b2bb38c1f98f007a9fa19b05de" "q-80768/selection/e5decc4150b760914cd0c276e29446374cd13b1976fc3c6778f33780269e9ce2" "q-80768/selection/1a2acfe5467bf9da155108d16669be8bf540403d734f98797845fdbd32db81c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80768" :question/id #uuid "6f18a33a-3190-5d7a-b7c8-c7f2c7cbfe22" :question/math-academy-id "q-80768" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz$,  find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,-1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2xy-z)\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2y)\\text{ }j-xk \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-1,-1) & =(\\,2(2)(-1)-(-1)\\,)\\text{ }i+(\\,{2}^{2}+2(-1)\\,)\\text{ }j-2k \\\\  & =-3\\,i+2\\,j-2\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80768/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80768"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80767/selection/cf652b2fe8cf1cd68aac885ad86c05bd32c065c4af19497970d905a3b10e62f8" :answer/id #uuid "2ebb3428-7f53-50ed-a8ee-090a3dffd16e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2y+7z-36=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80767/selection/59ce478a308a39ec04a8f7e08fe85b8510beb79534180500597b7aa3122369b9" :answer/id #uuid "1bec01be-310f-5003-be43-d5022a3ce1da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y+z-9=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80767/selection/bff2f2ef099dfed6bb8bf9266d0761512524b38c61bd26cbc927a0ebb0e56a8d" :answer/id #uuid "b43a55ad-3a12-5173-89ee-989adc571a06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x+2y+5z+7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80767/selection/2f0fb463479ca414ff06c046e3de1d48b5ea8bed7067546205e0a17943bb5f4f" :answer/id #uuid "d983287a-a2c3-5613-828e-6f591e363b71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x+y+z-23=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80767/selection/f572f9fab1c043df69c2d4c72455b1612369cc8f30f694517b3199e47a946d20" :answer/id #uuid "5a92898c-6e8c-5922-b567-63b181721199" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2y+5z-28=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80767/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a02bdb1-323f-55ed-888b-c4cac8abc19a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80767/selection/f572f9fab1c043df69c2d4c72455b1612369cc8f30f694517b3199e47a946d20" :answer-field/choices ["q-80767/selection/cf652b2fe8cf1cd68aac885ad86c05bd32c065c4af19497970d905a3b10e62f8" "q-80767/selection/59ce478a308a39ec04a8f7e08fe85b8510beb79534180500597b7aa3122369b9" "q-80767/selection/bff2f2ef099dfed6bb8bf9266d0761512524b38c61bd26cbc927a0ebb0e56a8d" "q-80767/selection/2f0fb463479ca414ff06c046e3de1d48b5ea8bed7067546205e0a17943bb5f4f" "q-80767/selection/f572f9fab1c043df69c2d4c72455b1612369cc8f30f694517b3199e47a946d20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80767" :question/id #uuid "eb777a66-6534-5731-b839-dbf8d0d1d605" :question/math-academy-id "q-80767" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=xy-yz-xz$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,3,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,3,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(y-z)\\text{ }i+(x-z)\\text{ }j+(-y-x)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,3,4) & =(3-4)\\text{ }i+(2-4)\\text{ }j+(-3-2)k \\\\  & =-1\\text{ }i-2\\text{ }j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,3,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,-2,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-2)-2(y-3)-5(z-4) & =0 \\\\ -x-2y-5z+28 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+5z-28 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80767/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80767"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37602"] :question/problem "Consider the surface $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}+yz)=3.$ Given that $n=⟨a,b,c⟩$ is a non-zero normal vector to the surface at the point $(e,{e}^{2},-e),$ what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define  $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}+yz).$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=3.$  \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(e,{e}^{2},-e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}+yz))i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}+yz))j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}+yz))k \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+yz}\\cdot 6{x}^{2})i+(\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+yz}\\cdot z)j+(\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+yz}\\cdot y)k \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{3}+yz}\\text{ }i+\\frac{z}{2{x}^{3}+yz}\\text{ }j+\\frac{y}{2{x}^{3}+yz}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(e,{e}^{2},-e) & =\\frac{6{e}^{2}}{2{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}(-e)}\\text{ }i+\\frac{(-e)}{2{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}(-e)}\\text{ }j+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}(-e)}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{e}\\text{ }i-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{e}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{6}{e},\\,-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{e}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩=⟨\\frac{6}{e},\\,-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{e}⟩.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{(\\frac{6}{e})}{(-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}})}=-6e.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-80783/selection/c7aebd2dba439f34715e2a87d91a1319e71afc06c6dc4ed27ae9f89dabc572f4" :answer/id #uuid "f07fb92c-6f6e-5354-a818-c05e6c6e8452" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x+y+z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80783/selection/b4f80bea036988d45545b8ea21432b208642b08650ef2c5410351096fbc159c5" :answer/id #uuid "c20f4153-30c7-57e2-9616-cfdcb540b13d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x+4y+z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80783/selection/e8dcdb87d32390337699782faacadfe62b8eb4d238e9473420a321d577c1a3a4" :answer/id #uuid "96c43a29-50a8-5896-ae2a-deef6550cf60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+y+z=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80783/selection/0a9b8377c3dd53aa44da68085ea3a460c9cd4392072ee43bdd22508d86387177" :answer/id #uuid "544e5842-2576-5766-973b-9a3ac8f91e41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-4y+2z=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80783/selection/dd37bc08b025f5063f531187cd26cf513be74045d1ef0e0df880e1587848ff82" :answer/id #uuid "b78226b4-eb24-5df6-90f9-bcc2be8523c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2y+z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80783/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f14ab69-a393-5252-b5e0-26b068897bcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80783/selection/b4f80bea036988d45545b8ea21432b208642b08650ef2c5410351096fbc159c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-80783/selection/c7aebd2dba439f34715e2a87d91a1319e71afc06c6dc4ed27ae9f89dabc572f4" "q-80783/selection/b4f80bea036988d45545b8ea21432b208642b08650ef2c5410351096fbc159c5" "q-80783/selection/e8dcdb87d32390337699782faacadfe62b8eb4d238e9473420a321d577c1a3a4" "q-80783/selection/0a9b8377c3dd53aa44da68085ea3a460c9cd4392072ee43bdd22508d86387177" "q-80783/selection/dd37bc08b025f5063f531187cd26cf513be74045d1ef0e0df880e1587848ff82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80783" :question/id #uuid "b91db3f9-c0e4-5574-95c9-b2372b5528a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-80783" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z{x}^{3}=-1+x{y}^{2}.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(1,-2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z{x}^{3} & =-1+x{y}^{2} \\\\ z{x}^{3}-x{y}^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=z{x}^{3}-x{y}^{2}$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-1.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,-2,3):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z{x}^{3}-x{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{x}^{3}-x{y}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{x}^{3}-x{y}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}z-{y}^{2})\\text{ }i-2xy\\text{ }j+{x}^{3}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,-2,3) & =(3(1)^{2}(3)-(-2)^{2})\\text{ }i-2(1)(-2)\\text{ }j+(1)^{3}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =5\\,i+4\\,j+1\\,k \\\\  & =⟨5,4,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-2,3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-(-2),\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨5,4,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+2,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 5(x-1)+4(y+2)+(z-3) & =0 \\\\ 5x+4y+z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80783/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80783"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36765/selection/dc07dba82590064b2e7b17edc1159bd44383c00ce69a2dd5ba41eb5e6dd5ea7f" :answer/id #uuid "d888d260-9410-55a2-8b34-547df07accd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2y-2z-12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36765/selection/88b2bf227278f750c3501eca9aa98e7e883db7f942c8b87786670f078c62e633" :answer/id #uuid "4efe22cf-f0ea-546a-989c-af7932619bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4y+z+6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36765/selection/e44bcd4910f939adcdfce09a14a0903626bb2f4db42be9bdc48566a250aa81aa" :answer/id #uuid "ea0eecca-cda2-5d59-8f2b-0fcbb148a3dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y+2z+4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36765/selection/5880b55f2e4d9f0e80f77220afe31a004c9bcd8716da8f576bdbd1dd1e32b51a" :answer/id #uuid "297e6c3f-228f-5395-bfd6-43c4eb37be64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-y+z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36765/selection/7c012b87fd66a0714d2a29f8d750ca511cfebcbf2430e5dd7cef0a859ed2886f" :answer/id #uuid "1d218f7b-96c2-5c2f-8db7-e63838737fe2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y+2z-8=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36765/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a852c8f-8672-5100-a6bf-df90456d1ce5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36765/selection/e44bcd4910f939adcdfce09a14a0903626bb2f4db42be9bdc48566a250aa81aa" :answer-field/choices ["q-36765/selection/dc07dba82590064b2e7b17edc1159bd44383c00ce69a2dd5ba41eb5e6dd5ea7f" "q-36765/selection/88b2bf227278f750c3501eca9aa98e7e883db7f942c8b87786670f078c62e633" "q-36765/selection/e44bcd4910f939adcdfce09a14a0903626bb2f4db42be9bdc48566a250aa81aa" "q-36765/selection/5880b55f2e4d9f0e80f77220afe31a004c9bcd8716da8f576bdbd1dd1e32b51a" "q-36765/selection/7c012b87fd66a0714d2a29f8d750ca511cfebcbf2430e5dd7cef0a859ed2886f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36765" :question/id #uuid "f3c1d374-96d3-54c1-935f-ec0d84c2144f" :question/math-academy-id "q-36765" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${x}^{2}=-xyz.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(4,2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =-xyz \\\\ {x}^{2}+xyz & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xyz$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(4,2,-2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2x+yz)\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(4,2,-2) & =(2(4)+2(-2))\\text{ }i+4(-2)\\text{ }j+4(2)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i-8j+8\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,-8,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(4,2,-2)\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-2,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,-8,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-2,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-4)+(-8)(y-2)+8(z+2) & =0 \\\\ 4x-8y+8z+16 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+2z+4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36765/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36765"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102718/selection/b04e4a57d5cfa105c05c8485edd1758869e784e6d64cd8afa6fe6441dd30dce0" :answer/id #uuid "b73da979-af4c-5653-a544-fa0ae63c8eab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x-y+{e}^{-1}z+4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102718/selection/9284690ccb0fc5b3b3a379bccbda58c26f56f8080f77d3fb9e056057b7369de7" :answer/id #uuid "99906516-d28a-5c24-b33e-ee5e0e3f7084" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x-{e}^{-1}y-z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102718/selection/482e8833c58f76781262c69a04ef9fe15d7485fa395e23105494c37543014af3" :answer/id #uuid "90d34227-dbaa-5aba-8d44-325bedfd326c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ex-2y+{e}^{-1}z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102718/selection/5765d45e9b2331ffa42938de3e5e2b9e69daa94133663b16667a19ce76fd6ddb" :answer/id #uuid "0666a840-b143-5d3c-9258-be0543aa4fc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ex-2y+ez-6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102718/selection/f52412d0e72dc0a0b43dbdb51d314d03936cc02079ffc61352797a0a233883b8" :answer/id #uuid "5abe9e1b-3982-5e26-9996-01d4c0f9256a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x-y+ez+6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102718/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6352a73b-867f-559a-865d-8ddffc50608f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102718/selection/b04e4a57d5cfa105c05c8485edd1758869e784e6d64cd8afa6fe6441dd30dce0" :answer-field/choices ["q-102718/selection/b04e4a57d5cfa105c05c8485edd1758869e784e6d64cd8afa6fe6441dd30dce0" "q-102718/selection/9284690ccb0fc5b3b3a379bccbda58c26f56f8080f77d3fb9e056057b7369de7" "q-102718/selection/482e8833c58f76781262c69a04ef9fe15d7485fa395e23105494c37543014af3" "q-102718/selection/5765d45e9b2331ffa42938de3e5e2b9e69daa94133663b16667a19ce76fd6ddb" "q-102718/selection/f52412d0e72dc0a0b43dbdb51d314d03936cc02079ffc61352797a0a233883b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102718" :question/id #uuid "61373bd7-6020-5bb2-b647-c3731f4fac66" :question/math-academy-id "q-102718" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z{e}^{x}+xy={x}^{2}.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(-1,1,2e).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z{e}^{x}+xy & ={x}^{2} \\\\ z{e}^{x}+xy-{x}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=z{e}^{x}+xy-{x}^{2}$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,1,2e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z{e}^{x}+xy-{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{e}^{x}+xy-{x}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{e}^{x}+xy-{x}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{x}+y-2x)\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j+{e}^{x}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,1,2e) & =((2e){e}^{-1}+1-2(-1))\\text{ }i+(-1)\\text{ }j+{e}^{-1}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =5\\,i-j+{e}^{-1}\\,k \\\\  & =⟨5,-1,{e}^{-1}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,1,2e)\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2e⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨5,-1,{e}^{-1}⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2e⟩ & =0 \\\\ 5(x+1)+(-1)(y-1)+{e}^{-1}(z-2e) & =0 \\\\ 5x-y+{e}^{-1}z+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102718/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102718"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102711/selection/b379a0316432f85a5b14f67f92790526d7d3fe4387303dde38a6a6a518198a6f" :answer/id #uuid "6b7a9547-6d52-54e9-9aab-3d6b32281afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4y-3z+15=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102711/selection/a0d47d7db5d36ff7b59c6cd53347d7759c66a4f6ac4c2ec43cd27eb37877fc1b" :answer/id #uuid "8d22379f-ff10-5dba-9bcb-c870b0b45323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-y+2z-10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102711/selection/bca003d28b977bc3d655365e5e05eedc909eab27ad83b9b45f993d27a9a76376" :answer/id #uuid "4ca43c0d-7fe2-5755-87ef-42cf6289c5c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+4y+5z-18=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102711/selection/b8b67cb286611f95dad23dbec250c9ff1a4230a19f93716df98ba8f8578296b7" :answer/id #uuid "563941e3-a9cc-5331-a246-1a6373b6d27b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-y+5z-12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102711/selection/34247d4c3263d632938ee5740ba47697a8373f544e7eb06cb868f703344e0ad1" :answer/id #uuid "fd142c72-f441-519a-a7d9-da7c1727a520" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+3y+z+12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102711/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ccf80b9-7cda-5bb3-8597-0bf687682fd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102711/selection/bca003d28b977bc3d655365e5e05eedc909eab27ad83b9b45f993d27a9a76376" :answer-field/choices ["q-102711/selection/b379a0316432f85a5b14f67f92790526d7d3fe4387303dde38a6a6a518198a6f" "q-102711/selection/a0d47d7db5d36ff7b59c6cd53347d7759c66a4f6ac4c2ec43cd27eb37877fc1b" "q-102711/selection/bca003d28b977bc3d655365e5e05eedc909eab27ad83b9b45f993d27a9a76376" "q-102711/selection/b8b67cb286611f95dad23dbec250c9ff1a4230a19f93716df98ba8f8578296b7" "q-102711/selection/34247d4c3263d632938ee5740ba47697a8373f544e7eb06cb868f703344e0ad1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102711" :question/id #uuid "58e862d4-ec1e-593c-943b-eb5a01ae4391" :question/math-academy-id "q-102711" :question/problem "Consider the surface $xy{z}^{2}=6-z.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(1,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{z}^{2} & =6-z \\\\ xy{z}^{2}+z & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+z$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=6.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(y{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+(x{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+(2xyz+1)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,2) & =(1)(2)^{2}\\text{ }i+(1)(2)^{2}\\text{ }j+(2(1)(1)(2)+1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i+4j+5\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,4,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,4,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)+4(y-1)+5(z-2) & =0 \\\\ 4x+4y+5z-18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102711/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102711"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3368"] :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z) = x^2+y^2+z^2,$ find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\! f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(x_0,y_0,z_0) =(2,-2,1)\\mathbin{:}$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}\\,i+{f}_{y}\\,j+{f}_{z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j+2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-2,1) & =2(2)\\text{ }i+2(-2)\\text{ }j+2(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i-4\\,j+2\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-4\\,,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-(-2),\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)-4(y+2)+2(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 4x-4y+2z-18 & =0 \\\\ 2x-2y+z-9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6183"] :question/problem "Consider the surface $z^3y^2 =x^2-5.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to this surface at the point $(-1,2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{3}{y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-5 \\\\ {z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z) = z^3y^2 - x^2,$ our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-5.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(-2x)\\text{ }i+2{z}^{3}y\\text{ }j+3{z}^{2}{y}^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,2,-1) & =(-2)(-1)\\text{ }i+2(-1)^{3}(2)\\text{ }j+3(-1)^{2}(2)^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2\\,i-4j+12\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,2,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-2,\\,z-(-1)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-4,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-2,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)-4(y-2)+12(z+1) & =0 \\\\ 2x-4y+12z+22 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+6z+11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
